      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### How the data gets here\n\n1. Every model call in the demos goes through **`track()`** (`src/meter.ts`). It times the call, reads the tokens from the vendor's `usage` field and prices them with `src/prices.ts`.\n2. When `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` is set in `.env`, `track()` also sends **OpenTelemetry** data to this container: one **span** per model call (stored in **Tempo**) and **metrics** for tokens, cost, latency and routing decisions (stored in **Prometheus**).\n3. This dashboard reads them back. Each demo run is a short process that sends its numbers when it finishes: wait about 30 seconds after a run, then refresh.\n\nEvery number is tagged with the **run** name (`2026-11-09_13-59-04_p1` = date, time, what ran). Pick it in the **run** menu at the top."
      },
      "id": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "datasource": null,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 13,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 11,
        "h": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### How to read it\n\n- **Summary** (Project 1 runs): the strong model alone on every failure (**before**) vs. `route(task)` on the same failures (**after**). Jev answers alone when it is sure; the rest go to an LLM.\n- **By model**: one row per model and role. *before* = strong model alone \u00b7 *after* = calls made inside `route(task)` \u00b7 *alone, for the comparison* = the other LLMs answering on their own.\n- **typical**: half the calls were faster, half slower \u00b7 **slow (1 in 20)**: 19 of 20 calls were faster, 1 in 20 slower.\n- **confidence**: Jev's is *calibrated* (trained so 0.8 is right about 8 times in 10). The LLMs' is *self-reported* (the model rated itself when asked).\n- Costs come from the price table in `src/prices.ts`. Other runs (race, bench, p2, p3, edges) appear in **By model** with their own role; the Summary stays empty for them."
      },
      "id": 2
    },
